.TH PIXLOG 1 "2026-07-31" "pixlog 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pixlog \- Git-compatible provenance layer for image assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pixlog
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pixlog
stores image media and provenance alongside Git while Git continues to own the
index, commits, branches, merges, and remotes. Git commits contain small PixLog
pointers and working trees contain the original image bytes.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize PixLog integration in the current Git repository.
.TP
.B track
Add image path patterns to the repository tracking policy.
.TP
.B status
Show repository and tracked image state.
.TP
.B diff
Compare working, staged, or committed image states.
.TP
.B inspect
Inspect an image and its PixLog metadata.
.TP
.B verify
Verify tracked media and provenance integrity.
.TP
.B doctor
Check repository configuration and object availability.
.TP
.B help
Show the complete command list and command usage.
.SH GIT INTEGRATION
When
.B git-pixlog
is available on PATH,
.B git pixlog
invokes the same command surface. Run
.B pixlog install
inside a repository to configure PixLog's Git integration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .pixlog.toml
Repository tracking and policy configuration.
.TP
.I .git/pixlog/
Local object storage, journals, locks, and integration state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-pixlog (1)
